{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1045 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "719e518b67e8e22db055455cf269aacfcfb0bae29d98a2411f082a32a5ac39f4" :edb/db-before-t 1044 :edb/db-after-t 1045 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534357 50 #inst "2026-10-06T16:49:37.508Z" 13194139534357 true] [17592186092019 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/e8ff769df4089e6ed9a47d56d7317acf41b8aef6a255abc705c0e7ec31a446ea.png)\n\nConsider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534357 true] [17592186092019 1100 "Consider the shaded region $D$ shown above. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/db07fd70ec06ccd7ac9258c2f4c75f22.png)" 13194139534357 false] [17592186092019 1145 "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = \\mid \\det(T) \\mid \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T$, we get\n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 - 2 \\cdot (-1) = 10\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea(T(D)) &= \\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & \\cdot Area(D) \\\\ = & 10\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 60\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534357 false] [17592186092019 1145 "Recall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = 4 \\cdot 2 -  2 \\cdot (-1) = 10.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|\\,10\\,|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =60.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534357 true] [17592186092020 1100 "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5)$, and $(-2,1)$. What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T$, given below?\n$\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534357 false] [17592186092020 1100 "A triangle $D$ has vertices $(1,1)$, $(4,5),$ and $(-2,1).$ What is the area of the image of $D$ under the action of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ with the standard matrix $T,$ given below?\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}-7 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534357 true] [17592186092020 1145 "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13992537/assets/ee8f0cf16983d87fa505303ed6372a3f389518d05b3e13f2e9e2121038792b84.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = |\\det(T)| \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6.\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 -  5 \\cdot (-2) = -11.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{Area}(T(D)) & =|det(T)|\\cdot \\text{Area}(D) \\\\  & =|-11|\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =66.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534357 true] [17592186092020 1145 "First, let's sketch our region:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/989/Source/Images/6c06e31f3407ba3e54c61c5b222b6d9d.png)\n\nRecall that for any linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$, we have the following connection between the area of $D$ and the area of the image $\\mathbf{T}(D)$ under the action of $\\mathbf{T}$:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(\\mathbf{T}(D)) = \\mid \\det(T) \\mid \\cdot \\text{Area}(D)\n$$\n\nFrom the diagram, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{Area}(D) = \\dfrac{1}{2} \\cdot 3 \\cdot 4 = 6\n$$\n\nComputing the determinant of $T$, we get\n\n$$\n\\det(T) = (-7) \\cdot 3 - 5 \\cdot (-2) = -11\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nArea(T(D)) &= \\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & \\cdot Area(D) \\\\ = & -11\\end{vmatrix}\\cdot 6 \\\\\n&= 66\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534357 false] [17592186092074 1100 "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139534357 false] [17592186092074 1100 "What is the area scale factor of the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ that is given by its standard matrix \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534357 true] [17592186092074 1145 "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $\\mid \\det(T) \\mid$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}det(T) & &= & 2 \\cdot 4 - 3 \\cdot 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\mid 8 - 3 \\mid \\\\\n&= 5\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534357 false] [17592186092074 1145 "The area scale factor of a linear transformation $\\mathbf T$ with standard matrix $T$ is equal to $|\\det(T)|.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|det(T)| & =|2\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 1| \\\\  & =|8-3| \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534357 true] [17592186092174 1020 #edb/ref 17592186283979 13194139534357 true] [17592186092174 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284000 13194139534357 true] [17592186092174 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284004 13194139534357 true] [17592186092174 1020 #edb/ref 17592186284038 1319